@startuml "Adapter - Iteration (Homework) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Adapter — homework 2, and the method that cannot be adapted


interface Iterator <<Target>> {
  + hasNext() : boolean
  + next() : T
  + remove()
}

interface Cursor <<Adaptee>> {
  + hasMoreElements() : boolean
  + nextElement() : T
}

class ArrayCursor
class CursorIteratorAdapter <<Adapter>>

Iterator <|.. CursorIteratorAdapter
Cursor <|.. ArrayCursor
CursorIteratorAdapter o--> "1" Cursor

note right of CursorIteratorAdapter
  hasNext and next map cleanly.

  <b>remove maps onto nothing.</b> A Cursor
  has no notion of removal, and no
  translation invents one.
end note

note as N1
  GoF, p. 141: how useful an adapter is
  depends on how much of the Target the
  adaptee can support.

  The honest answer is to <b>throw</b>. The
  tempting one is to do nothing quietly,
  and hand back a collection the caller
  believes it has modified.
end note

@enduml
